<title>RUSSIA: Russian 231-day T-bill tranche yields 32.13 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 231-day T-bill tranche yields 32.13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A new 231-day tranche of the Russian GKO discount Treasury bill series 22060 yielded an average 32.13 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>The issue closed at 83.04 to yield 32.13 percent on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the yield would be in a 31.97-33.70 percent range.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number	     22060 (additional tranche)</p>
<p>    Issue volume		4.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations	     1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)	    7.37 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)	    3.50 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds		    2.91 trln</p>
<p>    Average price	    83.10 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price  82.95 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield	    32.13 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield 32.48 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			231 day</p>
<p>    Issue date		 Jan 29, 1997</p>
<p>    Maturity date	    Sept 17, 1997</p>
<p>    Original issue date    Nov 27, 1996</p>
<p>The finance ministry is repaying about 6.63 trillion roubles in a maturing issue of six-month T-bills (series 22040) on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It will also offer a new four trillion rouble tranche of six-month T-bills (series 22065) and a new four trillion rouble tranche of OFZ interest-bearing bonds (series 24010).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
